% BGM Lab publications. This file is the single source for the Publications page,
% the "Latest publications" list on the homepage, and the tutorial list on the
% Workshops page. The fields follow the same conventions as nikolasekulovski.com,
% so entries can be copied between the two files.
%
% Add a paper by pasting its BibTeX here (journal site, Google Scholar, Zotero).
% Write the title in sentence case, as it should appear; braces are optional.
% Within a year, papers appear in the order of this file.
%
% Fields the website uses on top of the usual ones:
%   doi       -> "Paper" button (or `url` if there is no DOI)
%   preprint  -> "Preprint" button (a URL or a DOI)
%   pdf, code, data, osf, tutorial, blog, slides -> buttons with those names
%   pubstate  -> submitted | accepted | inpress
%                Papers with a pubstate are listed under "Forthcoming", without a year.
%                Remove the line once the paper is out.
%   note      -> a short line under the reference
%   keywords  -> add "tutorial" to list the paper on the Workshops page
% Keep each of these extra fields on one line; they are stripped from the
% "BibTeX" box visitors can copy. Lab members (data/team.yml) are shown in bold.

